WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.408
The school Week Three outline joins peripheral IV, tibial IO and timed twelve-lead acquisition. Its Wednesday discussions use prolonged vomiting with difficult veins and chest pressure with previous myocardial infarction.
学校第3周把外周静脉、胫骨骨内通路及限时十二导联采集连在一起。周三讨论包括持续呕吐且静脉困难的患者，以及既往心肌梗死后出现胸部压迫感的患者。

00:00:15.408 --> 00:00:27.792
This lab uses new cases with different ages and evolving observations to rehearse those objectives. These are not recovered school test questions or an answer key to the Simulation Channel.
本实训以年龄及后续变化不同的原创案例演练这些目标。它们不是恢复出来的学校试题，也不是Simulation Channel的答案。

00:00:27.792 --> 00:00:41.928
Before a planned first intervention, ask what else could explain the findings. After each intervention, name what changed, what should have changed and what got worse. Say the reasoning so that a partner can challenge it.
在计划中的首次干预前，问还有什么能解释这些发现。每次干预后，都说清实际变了什么、原应改变什么，以及什么变坏了。应把推理说出来，让搭档能够提出质疑。

00:00:41.928 --> 00:00:54.552
These pauses are brief cognitive checks, not permission to delay immediate lifesaving care. Simulation practice and a completed reading panel do not replace the actual school device checkoffs.
这些是简短的认知核查，不是延误立即救命照护的理由。完成模拟及阅读面板，也不能替代学校实际器材签核。

00:00:54.552 --> 00:01:10.440
A forty-six-year-old adult has vomited for three days and taken very little fluid. The pulse is one hundred eighteen, blood pressure ninety-two over fifty-eight and respiratory rate twenty-four. The hands are cool and sitting up produces dizziness.
一名46岁成人呕吐三天，饮水很少。脉搏每分钟118次，血压92/58，呼吸每分钟24次。双手凉，坐起时头晕。

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:22.944
Begin with the primary assessment and immediate support. Determine whether vomiting threatens the airway, whether breathing is effective and whether the circulation findings are persistent and credible.
先做初级评估及即时支持。判断呕吐是否威胁气道、呼吸是否有效，以及循环发现是否持续而可信。

00:01:22.944 --> 00:01:37.680
A saturation of ninety-seven percent does not demonstrate adequate tissue oxygen delivery. Flow, hemoglobin and tissue demand still matter; repeat patient assessment instead of declaring the circulation normal.
血氧饱和度97%并不证明组织供氧足够。血流、血红蛋白及组织需求仍重要；应重新评估患者，不能据此宣布循环正常。

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:49.968
The small veins create a technical challenge, but the clinical question comes first: what indicated treatment needs access now, who is authorized to provide it and what can continue while access is prepared?
细小静脉造成技术困难，但临床问题应先回答：现在什么有指征的治疗需要通路，谁获准实施，准备通路时又能继续哪些照护？

00:01:49.968 --> 00:02:04.416
Vomiting supports volume loss but does not explain its own cause. Ask about abdominal pain, diarrhea, fever, blood, medicines, pregnancy possibility where relevant and the sequence of symptoms.
呕吐支持容量丢失，但不能解释呕吐本身的病因。应询问腹痛、腹泻、发热、出血、药物、适用时的妊娠可能，以及症状先后。

00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:19.896
Consider metabolic disease, infection, bleeding and cardiac illness as the findings justify. Do not recite an enormous differential that changes nothing; identify the important alternative and what evidence would make you act differently.
依发现考虑代谢病、感染、出血及心脏疾病。不要背诵一长串却不影响行动的鉴别诊断；应指出重要替代解释，以及什么证据会改变行动。

00:02:19.896 --> 00:02:31.440
Check glucose when indicated and reconcile the history with the examination. A person described as merely dehydrated may have an illness requiring a different treatment or destination.
有指征时检查血糖，并把病史与体检相互核对。被简单称为脱水的患者，可能患有需要不同治疗或目的地的疾病。

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:45.744
State a working explanation and its uncertainty. For example: volume depletion is likely, but I am checking for a metabolic or bleeding cause while maintaining support and preparing indicated access.
应说明工作解释及不确定性。例如：容量不足很可能存在，但在维持支持及准备有指征通路的同时，我还在检查代谢或出血原因。

00:02:45.744 --> 00:02:58.944
Assign a clinician to the patient rather than to the needle. That person maintains observations, responds to vomiting or deterioration and keeps conveyance moving while another person prepares access.
应安排一人负责患者，而不是所有人都只盯着针。此人持续观察，处理呕吐或恶化，并在另一人准备通路时推动转运。

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:11.856
Explain the route, purpose and relevant discomfort, and obtain the applicable consent. Check allergy, relevant access restrictions and the reason the chosen limb and vein are suitable.
应解释通路、目的及相关不适，并取得适用同意。核对过敏、有关通路限制，以及所选肢体和静脉为何合适。

00:03:11.856 --> 00:03:25.776
Prepare the actual catheter, connection, flush and securement so that a successful insertion can immediately become a protected usable system. Missing equipment encourages contamination and interruption.
准备好实际留置针、连接、冲管及固定用品，使成功穿刺后可立即形成受保护且可用的系统。器材缺失容易造成污染及中断。

00:03:25.776 --> 00:03:37.032
Agree on when attempts stop and help is requested. Follow the actual policy for attempt limits; do not import an invented universal number from a different device or service.
事先约定何时停止尝试并请求帮助。次数限制应依真实政策，不能从不同器材或服务体系搬来一个虚构的通用数字。

00:03:37.032 --> 00:03:50.592
On the trainer, identify the proposed vessel before exposing the sharp. Describe its course and usable segment, then palpate for depth, compressibility and refill using the trained method.
在训练模型上，应先确认拟用血管，再暴露锐器。描述走向及可用段，然后用受训方法触诊深度、可压缩性及再充盈。

00:03:50.592 --> 00:04:02.280
A visible blue line alone is not sufficient identification, and a nearby pulse belongs in your assessment. Do not insert into an uncertain structure because the patient needs a quick result.
仅看到一条蓝线不足以确认血管，附近搏动也应纳入判断。不能因为急需结果，就向不确定结构穿刺。

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:15.264
Match the vein to the actual catheter and therapy, preserving distal options when suitable. A poor distal vein is not automatically the right choice merely because distal first is a useful general principle.
应让静脉、真实留置针及治疗相匹配，适合时保留远端以外的后续选择。先远端虽是有用原则，也不代表质量差的远端静脉必然最好。

00:04:15.264 --> 00:04:29.256
If the vein collapses or the landmarks remain uncertain, stop and reassess. Positioning, appropriate assistance and an alternative authorized plan are safer than repeatedly fishing through tissue.
若静脉塌陷或定位仍不确定，应停下来重评。适当摆位、求助及改用获准方案，比在组织中反复探找更安全。

00:04:29.256 --> 00:04:41.688
Use the complete peripheral workflow taught earlier in the week. Maintain hand hygiene, appropriate protection, the required skin preparation and drying, and a no-touch approach to critical parts.
应使用本周前课教授的完整外周流程：手卫生、适当防护、规定皮肤消毒及干燥，并避免触碰关键部位。

00:04:41.688 --> 00:04:55.416
Use the actual catheter instructions and school-supervised technique. Flashback, threading and safety activation differ between products, so a remembered angle or movement from another catheter is not enough.
操作应依真实留置针说明及学校督导技术。不同产品的回血、送管及安全启动不同，不能仅凭另一款导管记下的角度或动作。

00:04:55.416 --> 00:05:09.840
If the prepared site or connection is contaminated, identify the break and restore the appropriate clean or aseptic state before proceeding. Do not narrate an ideal sequence while physically continuing a contaminated one.
若已准备部位或连接受到污染，应指出中断并恢复所需清洁或无菌状态，再继续。不能口述理想流程，手上却继续污染后的操作。

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:22.176
Confirm function using the authorized method, secure the system and assess during actual delivery. A catheter in the skin is not proof that the prescribed treatment has entered the circulation.
应以获准方法确认功能、固定系统，并在真实给入时持续观察。皮肤内有导管，并不证明规定治疗已经进入循环。

00:05:22.176 --> 00:05:34.752
During the simulated flush the patient reports pain and swelling appears around the site. Stop delivery and assess the patient, connection and local tissues rather than forcing more volume through resistance.
模拟冲管时，患者说疼痛，部位周围出现肿胀。应停止给入，评估患者、连接及局部组织，不能遇阻后强推更多液体。

00:05:34.752 --> 00:05:50.016
Distinguish a local access complication from a systemic reaction or an unrelated change. The response depends on the actual substance and injury; an irritant or vesicant problem requires its specific escalation pathway.
应区分局部通路并发症、全身反应及无关变化。处理取决于真实物质及损伤；刺激性或发疱性物质问题，需要其特定升级路径。

00:05:50.016 --> 00:06:04.128
Do not automatically flush a suspected harmful extravasation or remove every device before checking the relevant plan. Some substance-specific management may use the existing access for aspiration or other treatment.
不能自动冲洗疑似有害外渗，也不能未核相关方案就一概拔除器材。某些物质的专门处理可能需利用原通路回抽或进一步治疗。

00:06:04.128 --> 00:06:16.632
Account for the actual amount delivered and any uncertainty. Restore patient support and choose the next appropriate route or help; the station is not passed simply because you once saw flashback.
应交代实际给入量及不确定部分。恢复患者支持，再选择适当通路或帮助；不能因为曾看到回血，就认为训练站已经成功。

00:06:16.632 --> 00:06:29.688
After an authorized simulated treatment, compare the same meaningful observations with the baseline. Record the dose or volume actually delivered and the time, not just the volume printed on the bag.
获准的模拟治疗后，应把相同且有意义的观察与基线比较。记录实际给入药量或液量及时间，不能只记液袋上印的容量。

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:42.816
Ask whether the intended perfusion target improved. A slightly higher pressure without improved mentation or peripheral findings is incomplete evidence and needs interpretation in the whole clinical picture.
应问目标灌注是否改善。血压略升，但意识或外周发现没有改善，只是不完整证据，需放回整个临床图景解释。

00:06:42.816 --> 00:06:56.808
Now add new breathlessness and crackles to the simulation. Reassess immediately for treatment-related harm or another cause, stop or modify the implicated treatment as indicated, and request appropriate help.
现在在模拟中加入新发气促及湿啰音。应立即重评治疗相关伤害或其他原因，按指征停止或调整有关治疗，并请求适当帮助。

00:06:56.808 --> 00:07:07.992
The correct response is not to finish a planned volume merely because it was initially reasonable. A treatment remains conditional on the patient and the current findings.
不能因为原计划最初合理，就坚持把预定液量输完。治疗始终以患者及当前发现为条件。

00:07:07.992 --> 00:07:20.760
The school asks when the difficult-vein patient might require tibial IO and includes an awake-IO exercise. Learn that decision, but do not treat the classroom scenario as unrestricted field authority.
学校要求讨论静脉困难者何时可能需胫骨IO，并安排清醒患者IO练习。应学会决策，但不能把课堂情境视为不受限的现场权限。

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:36.912
The checked current PCP independent branch is restricted to patients twelve or older in clearly hypovolemic cardiac arrest, with the stated critical fluid and failed or unavailable peripheral-access conditions. It is not a general dehydration pathway.
已核当前PCP独立路径，限制于12岁及以上、明确低血容量性心搏骤停，并符合规定的关键补液及外周通路失败或不可用条件；它不是一般脱水路径。

00:07:36.912 --> 00:07:50.640
The alternative described in the current procedure requires direct on-scene supervision by an ACP or higher clinician. A phone conversation alone does not become the on-scene supervision required by that branch.
当前规程另一路径要求ACP或更高级临床人员在现场直接督导。仅有电话沟通，不会自动满足这一路径的现场督导要求。

00:07:50.640 --> 00:08:05.448
Our awake patient therefore does not become independently eligible merely because a vein failed. State the actual authority and supervision before the simulated drill is prepared, and continue necessary support and conveyance.
因此，本例清醒患者不会仅因静脉失败就自动获得独立IO适用资格。准备模拟钻前，应说清真实权限及督导，同时继续必要支持及转运。

00:08:05.448 --> 00:08:20.808
Before the trainer is touched, identify the patient category and the exact branch of authority. Current D zero three prohibits PCP cannulation under twelve by any method; do not borrow a broader manufacturer age range.
触碰模型前，应说明患者类别及准确权限分支。当前D03禁止PCP以任何方法给12岁以下患者置管；不能借用厂商更宽的年龄范围。

00:08:20.808 --> 00:08:35.232
Screen the proposed limb and site using the full procedure and actual device instructions. Relevant fractures, local infection, previous attempts and uncertainty about landmarks must be resolved before insertion.
应按完整规程及真实器材说明筛查肢体和部位。相关骨折、局部感染、既往尝试及定位不确定，都应在置入前解决。

00:08:35.232 --> 00:08:48.192
The checked PCP pathway is tibial and permits two collective attempts, not two attempts for every provider. A failed or dislodged site is not simply recannulated as though nothing happened.
已核PCP路径限胫骨，合计允许两次尝试，不是每位人员各两次。失败或脱出的部位，不能当作没发生过一样重新置管。

00:08:48.192 --> 00:08:58.944
Use the actual school device and supervised landmarks. This rehearsal does not invent a needle length, insertion depth or pressure setting for an unidentified product.
应使用学校真实器材及督导定位。本演练不会给身份未明的产品虚构针长、置入深度或压力设置。

00:08:58.944 --> 00:09:11.016
The saved school case specifies zero point five milligrams per kilogram of lidocaine over sixty seconds before fluid. That is the source the student should recognize in the classroom discussion.
学校存档案例写的是利多卡因每公斤0.5毫克，60秒内给入后再补液。学生应能在课堂讨论中认出这一来源。

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:27.216
The checked current adult PR twelve regimen instead specifies forty milligrams over one hundred twenty seconds and a sixty-second dwell. The authority is the relevant ACP pathway or the permitted PCP under direct on-scene ACP supervision.
已核当前成人PR12则规定40毫克用120秒给入，再停留60秒。权限属于相应ACP路径，或获准PCP在ACP现场直接督导下实施。

00:09:27.216 --> 00:09:42.192
For arithmetic only, the school formula applied to sixty kilograms gives thirty milligrams. That calculation does not establish a complete regimen, an allowed maximum, product suitability or permission to administer it.
仅从算术看，学校公式用于60公斤得到30毫克。但这一计算并不确立完整方案、允许上限、产品适用性，也不构成给药权限。

00:09:42.192 --> 00:09:55.968
At the station, identify which approved protocol sheet the instructor is using before preparing simulated medication. Do not create a hybrid by combining the school weight-based dose with the current timing or the reverse.
训练站中，应先确认教师采用哪张批准方案，再准备模拟药物。不能把学校按体重剂量与当前时间拼接，反过来也不行。

00:09:55.968 --> 00:10:08.304
Use the actual procedure to verify placement and function before the planned delivery. A needle that feels stable or a patient who feels less pain is not by itself sufficient confirmation.
计划给入前，应按真实规程确认位置及功能。针看起来稳定，或患者觉得不那么痛，都不能单独作为充分确认。

00:10:08.304 --> 00:10:21.408
Monitor the limb and site during treatment, including pain, swelling, leakage and relevant distal findings. Secure the system so that moving the patient does not turn a working route into a displaced one.
治疗中应监测肢体及部位，包括疼痛、肿胀、渗漏及有关远端发现。应固定系统，避免搬运使可用通路移位。

00:10:21.408 --> 00:10:37.536
If abnormal swelling or severe pain raises concern for extravasation or compartment injury, stop the implicated delivery and obtain the appropriate urgent review. Do not compensate for poor flow by increasing pressure without reassessment.
若异常肿胀或剧痛提示外渗或筋膜室损伤，应停止有关给入并取得适当紧急评估。不能不重评，就靠增加压力补偿流量差。

00:10:37.536 --> 00:10:52.368
Hand over the route, site, attempt count, insertion time, actual medication and fluid delivered, response and complications. The receiving team needs the full route history, not simply IO present.
交接应包括途径、部位、尝试次数、置入时间、实际给入药液、反应及并发症。接收团队需要完整通路经过，而不只是“有IO”。

00:10:52.368 --> 00:11:05.256
A fifty-nine-year-old adult has twenty-five minutes of central pressure and nausea. There is a previous infarction, and the person says the sensation is similar. They are alert, cool and sweaty.
一名59岁成人胸部中央压迫感及恶心持续25分钟，既往心肌梗死，并说这次感觉相似。患者清醒，但皮肤凉且出汗。

00:11:05.256 --> 00:11:19.272
Assess and support the patient while promptly preparing a diagnostic-quality twelve-lead. A prior infarction raises concern, but the history still needs its timing, associated symptoms and relevant medicines.
应在评估及支持患者的同时，迅速准备具诊断质量的十二导联。既往梗死增加警惕，但仍需了解此次时间、伴随症状及相关药物。

00:11:19.272 --> 00:11:32.688
Ask what else could explain the presentation, including important dangerous alternatives when the findings suggest them. The question widens attention; it does not erase the need to act on likely acute coronary disease.
应问还有什么能解释表现，并在发现支持时考虑重要危险替代病因。这个问题是拓宽注意，不是取消对可能急性冠脉疾病采取行动。

00:11:32.688 --> 00:11:45.384
A previous tracing can help if promptly available, but searching for it must not delay current acquisition or indicated care. A normal-looking early trace also does not exclude acute coronary syndrome.
既往图若能迅速取得可帮助比较，但寻找旧图不能延误当前采集或有指征照护。早期图看似正常，也不能排除急性冠脉综合征。

00:11:45.384 --> 00:11:56.448
Explain why the chest electrodes and exposure are necessary, obtain appropriate consent and protect privacy with the least exposure compatible with correct placement.
应解释胸部电极及暴露的必要性，取得适当同意，并以不影响正确放置的最少暴露保护隐私。

00:11:56.448 --> 00:12:10.320
Prepare the skin and locate the anatomical landmarks. Position breast tissue respectfully when needed; do not place the precordial electrodes over breast tissue simply to avoid a clear explanation.
准备皮肤并找到解剖标志。需要时应尊重地处理乳房组织位置；不能为避免解释，就简单把胸前电极贴在乳房组织上。

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:22.728
One provider remains responsible for the patient and urgent indicated care while another acquires the tracing. If the patient deteriorates, announce the change and reprioritize together.
采图时仍应有一人负责患者及紧急有指征照护。若患者恶化，应立即报告变化，并共同重排优先级。

00:12:22.728 --> 00:12:35.640
Use actual patient identification and time on the real clinical trace. Training names and a simulated clock belong only to the trainer and must not become false clinical documentation.
真实临床心电图应使用实际患者身份及时间。训练姓名及模拟时钟仅用于模型，不能进入虚假临床记录。

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:51.744
Saved school seven G defines the target: a diagnostic-quality trace acquired and readable in under three minutes from patient contact, in a cooperative appropriate patient. The actual device checkoff and grading rubric remain separate source gaps.
学校存档7G明确目标：对合作且适合的患者，从接触患者起，不到三分钟内采得可读且具诊断质量的图。实际器材签核及评分表，仍是另外的来源缺口。

00:12:51.744 --> 00:13:05.280
Locate V one and V two in the fourth interspaces on the right and left sternal borders. Locate V four in the fifth interspace at the midclavicular line, then V three between V two and V four.
V1及V2分别位于第四肋间胸骨右缘和左缘。V4位于第五肋间锁骨中线，V3再放在V2与V4之间。

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:18.120
Place V five and V six horizontally level with V four at the appropriate anterior and midaxillary lines. Do not follow the downward slope of a rib or estimate the entire set by nipple position.
V5及V6应分别置于适当的腋前线及腋中线，与V4保持水平；不能沿肋骨向下倾斜，也不能以乳头位置估算整套电极。

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:32.664
Complete the limb connections and verify identity, signal quality and calibration. A fast unusable tracing does not meet a quality acquisition goal; note the reason for delay and repeat practice safely.
完成肢体连接并核对身份、信号质量及定标。很快却无法使用的图，不符合有质量采集目标；应记录延误原因，再安全练习。

00:13:32.664 --> 00:13:45.864
The monitor suddenly displays a very rapid irregular-looking pattern while the patient is shaking. Look at the person, assess pulse and perfusion, and inspect the signal rather than treating the screen alone.
患者发抖时，监护突然显示非常快且看似不规则的图形。应看患者、评估脉搏及灌注，并检查信号，不能只治疗屏幕。

00:13:45.864 --> 00:14:00.600
Compare simultaneous leads for recognizable underlying complexes, and check electrode contact, cables and motion. Artifact may coexist with real disease, so correcting it does not finish the clinical assessment.
应比较同步导联是否有可辨认的底层波群，并检查电极接触、导线及运动。伪差可与真实疾病并存，因此纠正伪差并不结束临床评估。

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:15.024
If the person becomes unresponsive and has no definite pulse, follow the arrest pathway without a prolonged troubleshooting delay. Uncertainty about one tracing is not a reason to ignore a changed patient category.
若患者无反应且无明确脉搏，应进入骤停路径，不能长时间排查器材而延误。对一张图有疑问，不是忽视患者类别改变的理由。

00:14:15.024 --> 00:14:29.808
When the patient is perfusing, correct the identified problem and reacquire a usable trace, preserving and explaining relevant originals. Do not label a dangerous rhythm artifact simply because the patient was initially awake.
患者有灌注时，应纠正已识别问题并重采可用图，保留及解释有意义的原图。不能仅因最初清醒，就把危险心律都说成伪差。

00:14:29.808 --> 00:14:42.744
Use the structured method from the seven G lessons: describe rate, regularity, atrial activity, the P-to-QRS relationship, QRS width and other relevant intervals before naming a rhythm.
应使用7G课的结构化方法：先描述频率、规则性、心房活动、P与QRS关系、QRS宽度及其他相关间期，再命名心律。

00:14:42.744 --> 00:14:57.696
For the diagnostic trace, examine contiguous lead patterns and the clinical context. The device interpretation is a prompt for review, not an independent diagnosis or authority to bypass the current pathway.
诊断图应观察相邻导联模式及临床背景。机器解释只是复核提示，不是独立诊断，也不赋予绕过当前路径的权限。

00:14:57.696 --> 00:15:12.696
Acute coronary disease may evolve or be present without a classic initial ST-elevation pattern. Repeat when symptoms or the condition change, and obtain the required expert interpretation and destination guidance.
急性冠脉疾病可逐渐演变，也可在首图没有典型ST抬高时已经存在。症状或病情变化时应重采，并取得所需专家解释及目的地指导。

00:15:12.696 --> 00:15:26.736
An extra lead set or an alternative position must be accurately labelled and communicated. Do not silently replace a standard electrode position and then interpret the result as an unchanged standard twelve-lead.
增加导联或采用替代位置时，必须准确标注并交代。不能悄悄改变标准电极位置，再把结果当作未改变的标准十二导联解释。

00:15:26.736 --> 00:15:39.840
While you compare leads, the patient becomes pale and nearly faints. The pulse feels weaker and the repeat blood pressure is substantially lower. Stop treating interpretation as the only task.
比较导联时，患者苍白并几乎晕厥，脉搏更弱，复测血压明显下降。此时不能再把读图当作唯一任务。

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:54.600
Reassess airway, breathing, circulation and consciousness, confirm the observations promptly and provide indicated support. Announce the change so the crew does not continue the previous stable-patient plan.
应重新评估气道、呼吸、循环及意识，迅速确认观察并提供有指征支持。应明确宣布变化，避免团队继续沿用先前稳定患者方案。

00:15:54.600 --> 00:16:07.728
Request appropriate advanced help and follow the current pathway for the actual rhythm and clinical state. A treatment requiring additional authority does not become independently allowed because the situation is frightening.
应请求适当高级帮助，并按真实心律和临床状态遵循当前路径。需要额外权限的治疗，不会因情况令人紧张就自动允许独立实施。

00:16:07.728 --> 00:16:20.352
If arrest occurs, move immediately to the arrest pathway. If a pulse remains, maintain the appropriate pulse-present plan and avoid assuming that every abnormal ECG requires a shock.
若发生骤停，应立即转骤停路径。若仍有脉搏，应维持适当的有脉搏方案，不能假定每种异常心电图都需要电击。

00:16:20.352 --> 00:16:32.112
Rehearse the assigned two-step blood-pressure method with a correct cuff and supported arm. A palpatory estimate helps guide the later inflation and avoid missing an auscultatory gap.
应使用正确袖带及有支撑的手臂，演练指定的两步血压法。先触诊估计可指导随后充气，并帮助避免遗漏听诊间隙。

00:16:32.112 --> 00:16:45.168
Compare a reliable pulse with the electrical rate. An electrical complex does not guarantee an effective stroke volume, and a weak irregular peripheral pulse may not equal every detected QRS.
应把可靠脉搏与电频率比较。一个电波群不保证有效搏出量，弱而不齐的外周脉搏也可能不对应每个检测到的QRS。

00:16:45.168 --> 00:16:57.528
Use pulse oximetry with signal quality and patient context. Poor perfusion and other limitations can affect the result; a plausible normal value does not rule out low flow or anemia.
脉搏血氧应结合信号质量及患者背景使用。低灌注等限制可影响结果；一个看似正常的数值，不能排除低血流或贫血。

00:16:57.528 --> 00:17:10.440
Record observations at meaningful times with posture, treatment and relevant device settings. Changing the method without saying so can create an apparent improvement that is only measurement variation.
应在有意义时点记录，并交代体位、治疗及相关器材设置。若改变方法却不说明，可能把测量差异误当改善。

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:25.824
For a simulated D ten label stating ten grams per one hundred millilitres, twelve point five grams corresponds to one hundred twenty-five millilitres. Show grams cancelling rather than jumping from a drug name to a memorized volume.
模拟D10标签为每100毫升10克时，12.5克对应125毫升。应展示克单位约去，不能仅从药名直接跳到记忆中的体积。

00:17:25.824 --> 00:17:41.544
For three hundred millilitres over ninety minutes, divide by one point five hours to obtain two hundred millilitres per hour. With a simulated twenty-drop-per-millilitre set, the gravity calculation is approximately sixty-seven drops per minute.
300毫升在90分钟内给入，除以1.5小时得到每小时200毫升。模拟管路滴系数为每毫升20滴时，重力滴速约每分钟67滴。

00:17:41.544 --> 00:17:57.360
Read the actual tubing factor and product concentration; neither follows from the bag size or the colour of the set. Gravity delivery varies, so verify actual flow and patient response rather than trusting one count indefinitely.
应读取真实管路滴系数及产品浓度；它们都不能从液袋大小或管路颜色推断。重力流量会变化，须核实际流量及患者反应，不能永远相信一次计数。

00:17:57.360 --> 00:18:11.688
These are original arithmetic exercises, not recommended treatment amounts for either case. Real administration still requires the correct patient, indication, authorized dose, route and reassessment plan.
这些是原创算术练习，不是给任一病例建议的治疗量。真实给入仍需要正确患者、指征、获准药量、途径及复评方案。

00:18:11.688 --> 00:18:23.880
Use SBAR for consultation or the required receiving-service structure. Lead with the active problem and urgency rather than making the listener reconstruct them from a long chronological story.
咨询可用SBAR，接收交接应依所需结构。应先说当前问题及紧急程度，不要让听者从冗长流水账中自行拼出重点。

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:38.472
For the access case, include the route and site, attempts, any failed or displaced access, actual fluid or medication delivered and the patient response. Do not imply that the full prepared volume entered.
通路病例应交代途径及部位、尝试次数、失败或脱出通路、实际给入药液，以及患者反应。不能暗示所有准备体积都已进入。

00:18:38.472 --> 00:18:53.760
For the chest case, include symptom onset, relevant history, serial observations, acquisition times, important ECG findings and any change. Identify any nonstandard electrode position or extra lead set.
胸痛病例应交代起病、相关病史、连续观察、采图时间、重要心电发现及变化。任何非标准电极位置或新增导联，都应说明。

00:18:53.760 --> 00:19:08.112
State the next specific need and confirm the receiver understood. Documentation should preserve the same facts, sequence, uncertainty and response; a polished handover must not hide a complication.
应说清下一项具体需要，并确认接收者理解。记录应保留相同事实、顺序、不确定性及反应；流利交接不能掩盖并发症。

00:19:08.112 --> 00:19:20.616
At the peripheral station, the partner observes the full chain and introduces one contamination or local-failure cue. A technically successful insertion is only one part of the performance.
外周站由搭档观察完整链，并加入一次污染或局部失败线索。穿刺技术成功只是表现的一部分。

00:19:20.616 --> 00:19:33.912
At the tibial station, verbalize authority, exclusions, attempt counting and the approved pain protocol before using the supervised trainer. Do not practice invasive procedures on yourself or a partner.
胫骨站应在使用督导模型前，口述权限、排除条件、次数统计及批准镇痛方案。不能在自己或搭档身上练习侵入操作。

00:19:33.912 --> 00:19:48.216
At the ECG station, rehearse the school contact-to-readable-trace target and check the complete electrode map. Add movement artifact after the first acquisition so that quality correction is observed rather than only described.
心电站应演练学校从接触到取得可读图的目标，并检查完整电极图。首次采集后加入运动伪差，让质量纠正真正可观察，而不只是口述。

00:19:48.216 --> 00:20:01.320
At the integrated station, change one clinical finding after an intervention. Require a revised plan and structured handover, not a repeated memorized script that ignores the new information.
整合站应在干预后改变一项临床发现，要求调整方案并结构化交接，不能重复背好的稿子而忽视新信息。

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:13.752
Describe what actually happened, including a missed cue or a helpful action. Avoid calling a learner careless or naturally talented when the important evidence is a specific step and its timing.
应描述真实发生的事，包括遗漏线索或有帮助的行动。关键证据是具体步骤及时间，不应只说某学生粗心或天生有天赋。

00:20:13.752 --> 00:20:26.688
Ask what information the learner had at the time and why the action seemed reasonable. This distinguishes a knowledge gap, a misleading cue, a device problem and a failure to re-evaluate.
应问当时掌握什么信息，以及为什么觉得该行动合理。这能区分知识缺口、误导线索、器材问题及未重新评估。

00:20:26.688 --> 00:20:41.136
Connect the step to its clinical consequence. For example, everyone preparing IO left vomiting unsupported, or a rapidly printed ECG was unusable because the precordial landmarks were guessed.
应把步骤与临床后果连接。例如所有人准备IO，导致呕吐无人支持；或心电图虽打印很快，却因猜胸前位置而无法使用。

00:20:41.136 --> 00:20:53.808
Choose one correction, repeat the relevant sequence and record whether the correction was observed. A positive discussion without a changed performance is not evidence that the skill is now reliable.
选择一项修正，重做相关顺序，并记录是否观察到修正。讨论气氛积极但表现未变，并不证明技能已经可靠。

00:20:53.808 --> 00:21:07.656
Use the physiology and reading lessons to explain why the decisions work: pressure is not flow, electrical activation is not guaranteed mechanical output, and infused water does not stay entirely in plasma.
应借生理及阅读课解释决策为何成立：压力不等于血流，电激动不保证机械输出，输进的水也不会全部留在血浆。

00:21:07.656 --> 00:21:20.712
Then demonstrate the complete sequence with the actual supervised training equipment. Explain the intervention, protect the route, verify function and reassess the patient after real or simulated delivery.
再使用真实督导训练器材展示完整顺序：解释干预、保护通路、确认功能，并在真实或模拟给入后重评患者。

00:21:20.712 --> 00:21:36.216
All eleven assigned Week Three reading rows now have paired explanatory guides in this course. Exact school editions, some linked activities, original PPT bodies and assessed station materials still require source confirmation.
本课程现在已为第3周全部十一条指定阅读提供中英对照解释性导读。但学校准确版本、部分链接活动、原始PPT正文及考核站材料，仍需来源确认。

00:21:36.216 --> 00:21:48.312
This is preparation, not a claim that the whole school week is certified complete. Bring unresolved device and protocol differences to the instructor, and keep the actual school assessment your own work.
这属于课前准备，不是宣布整周已认证完成。应把未解决的器材及方案差异交给教师核实，学校实际考核仍由你本人完成。
